From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0008] DeepSeek-V4-0731 thinking/effort defaults, parser mode
 sync, and tile-local argmax vocab clamp
 (port of haosdent/vllm#21, adapted to the c3046d1 base)

WHAT THIS FIXES. The DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 hosted-model contract expects
omitted thinking/enable_thinking to mean THINKING, not chat. On this tree
(as on the pre-#21 dsv4-flash-a100 branch) it means chat, and every
reasoning_effort other than "max"/"xhigh" silently collapses to the "high"
prefix with no low/minimal/medium distinction. A request that omits
thinking/enable_thinking therefore renders a generation prompt that ends
`</think>` instead of `<think>`. In agentic histories this desyncs the
parser (below) and is one driver of the "Let me..." phrase-lock loop: the
model repeats a stock reasoning opener because the prompt told it, via the
missing prefix, that it is not supposed to be thinking at all, then the
loop reinforces itself over subsequent turns.

Three independent changes, in provenance order:

1. `vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v4.py`, `vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v4_encoding.py`
   -- omitted thinking/enable_thinking now means thinking=True (matching the
   0731 template contract); reasoning_effort gains a real low/high/max
   three-way instead of collapsing everything but max/xhigh into "high".
   Port of vllm-project/vllm#50580 (merged upstream 2026-08-04).

2. `vllm/parser/deepseek_v4.py` -- `DeepSeekV4Parser.__init__` mirrors the
   same "omitted means thinking" default. Without this, a request with no
   thinking kwarg renders a thinking-mode prompt (change 1) but the parser
   still initializes its state machine in CONTENT, so the model's reasoning
   between the omitted `<think>`/`</think>` streams out as user-visible
   content instead of being suppressed -- which is what actually poisons the
   conversation history over long agentic contexts and degrades DSML
   tool-call emission on later turns.

3. `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/gumbel.py`,
   `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/rejection_sampler_utils.py` -- clamp the
   tile-local argmax to `vocab_size - 1` at three sites
   (`_gumbel_sample_kernel`, `_compute_local_logits_stats_kernel`,
   `_resample_kernel`). Each reduces over a BLOCK_SIZE-wide tile and forms
   `token_id = block_idx * BLOCK_SIZE + idx`; the out-of-vocab tail lanes of
   the last tile are loaded as -inf, so a degenerate all-(-inf/NaN) tile can
   settle the reduction on a tail lane and produce `token_id >= vocab_size`.
   Nothing downstream bounds a sampled token id, and DeepSeek-V4's hash-MoE
   router indexes `tid2eid[token_id * topk]` directly -- an out-of-range id
   reads past the table and faults every rank. Distinct bug from 0007 (which
   guards NaN rows feeding `tl.argmax` in a different pair of kernels,
   `_compute_global_target_argmax` and `_insert_resampled_kernel`); this
   clamp is unconditionally safe on its own, since an in-vocab argmax is
   unaffected and only an index already outside the vocabulary changes.
   Port of vllm-project/vllm#50843 (upstream PR, open at port time).

PROVENANCE AND WHY THIS IS ADAPTED RATHER THAN CHERRY-PICKED. Upstream PR
haosdent/vllm#21 bundles these three commits against the current tip of
dsv4-flash-a100, which has continued past the c3046d1 rebase point this
patch series pins. File line numbers there do not match this tree, but a
byte-for-byte diff of every touched region against our c3046d1 checkout
shows the surrounding code is identical -- only line offsets differ from
unrelated commits landing in between. This patch carries the same logic
renumbered for c3046d1, plus this rationale. haosdent/vllm#21 itself is
still in draft (marked "AI-assisted -- human review required" with an
unchecked review checklist) and change 1 traces to a third-party backport
(wtdcode/vllm-backport), not vllm-project directly -- treat the reasoning
above, not that PR's description, as the record of what was actually
verified before landing here.

Applies after 0007 in glob order; touches
`v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/rejection_sampler_utils.py` at different
functions than 0007 (no overlap) plus four files no other patch modifies.

